01:01:20.880 --> 01:01:27.780
At 17 minutes, 36 seconds, I am leaning up against Michael's doorframe, standing next to Toby.
在17分36秒的时候，我靠在迈克尔的门框上，站在托比旁边。

2092
01:01:28.040 --> 01:01:31.960
And you can see the beginning of my baby belly.
你可以看到我怀孕初期的小肚子。

2093
01:01:32.200 --> 01:01:33.480
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

2094
01:01:33.480 --> 01:01:34.580
Are you serious?
你是认真的吗？

2095
01:01:34.980 --> 01:01:35.800
I am serious.
我是认真的。

2096
01:01:35.800 --> 01:01:40.580
And I rewatched this episode with my daughter and I didn't say anything to her.
我和我女儿重温这一集的时候，我什么都没跟她说。

2097
01:01:40.580 --> 01:01:45.640
And as she was watching it with me, we got to the scene and she said, mom, is this when
当她和我一起看的时候，演到这一幕，她说，妈妈，这是你

2098
01:01:45.640 --> 01:01:47.040
you were pregnant with me?
怀我的时候吗？

2099
01:01:47.160 --> 01:01:48.720
And I said, it was.
我说，是的。

2100
01:01:49.060 --> 01:01:49.660
Look, Jenna.
看，珍娜。

2101
01:01:50.580 --> 01:01:51.820
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

2102
01:01:52.100 --> 01:01:56.440
And you have your hands in front of your stomach to kind of try to hide it.
而且你把手放在肚子前面，试图遮住它。

2103
01:01:56.540 --> 01:02:00.600
But Ange, I thought I could kind of see it earlier in the episode when you have your
但是安吉，我觉得我在这一集早些时候，当你第一次走到吉姆的办公桌前时，

2104
01:02:00.600 --> 01:02:02.560
first scene walking up to Jim's desk.
好像就看出点端倪了。

2105
01:02:02.800 --> 01:02:03.040
Really?
真的吗？

2106
01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:06.580
They tried to position you a little bit behind his computer screen.
他们试图让你稍微躲在他的电脑屏幕后面。

2107
01:02:06.580 --> 01:02:11.260
But maybe because I know I felt like I had a belly spot.
但也许是因为我知道，我觉得自己当时肚子已经显怀了。

2108
01:02:11.520 --> 01:02:16.080
Well, this will be the beginning of the belly tracking because we had to get really creative
好吧，这将是“肚子追踪”的开始，因为在接下来的几周里，

2109
01:02:16.080 --> 01:02:17.440
over the next few weeks.
我们必须得发挥创意了。

2110
01:02:17.720 --> 01:02:20.840
I'm ready to head back out to the forest, Angela.
我准备好回到森林里去了，安吉拉。

2111
01:02:21.400 --> 01:02:21.860
OK.
好的。

2112
01:02:22.360 --> 01:02:26.800
Because I have a lot to say about this scene where Michael finds some mushrooms growing
因为关于迈克尔发现树下长了一些蘑菇并开始吃它们的那个场景，

2113
01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:29.700
under a tree and he starts to eat them.
我有很多话要说。

2114
01:02:29.700 --> 01:02:33.820
And Dwight tackles him and forces them out of his mouth.
然后德怀特扑倒他，强迫他把蘑菇吐出来。

2115
01:02:34.520 --> 01:02:35.820
It's pretty amazing.
这太精彩了。

2116
01:02:36.120 --> 01:02:36.900
It's so great.
真是太棒了。

2117
01:02:37.180 --> 01:02:39.320
I had to know more about these mushrooMs.
我必须了解更多关于这些蘑菇的信息。

2118
01:02:39.660 --> 01:02:40.760
What'd you find out?
你查到了什么？

2119
01:02:41.200 --> 01:02:47.300
According to Dunderpedia, the species of mushroom that Michael was about to eat are called
根据《邓德百科》的记载，迈克尔当时要吃的蘑菇品种叫

2120
01:02:48.640 --> 01:02:49.840
Hyphaloma fasciculare.
束生沿丝伞。

2121
01:02:50.400 --> 01:02:52.060
I'm sure I got that wrong.
我肯定读错了。

2122
01:02:52.220 --> 01:02:53.820
I would never be able to say that.
我绝对念不出那个词。

2123
01:02:54.060 --> 01:02:57.660
They are more commonly known as the clustered wood lover.
它们更常见的名字是“簇生木腐菌”。

2124
01:02:58.140 --> 01:02:58.580
OK.
好吧。

2125
01:02:58.580 --> 01:03:00.580
I deep dived on these mushrooMs.
我深入研究了这些蘑菇。

2126
01:03:00.860 --> 01:03:02.360
I'm guessing they grow on wood.
我猜它们长在木头上。

2127
01:03:02.680 --> 01:03:03.680
They do.
确实如此。

2128
01:03:04.000 --> 01:03:10.120
It is a type of mushroom and they grow on rotten trees, stumps or trunks.
这是一种蘑菇，它们生长在腐烂的树木、树桩或树干上。

2129
01:03:10.440 --> 01:03:16.280
The taste is very bitter if you eat them raw, but they are not bitter if you cook them.
生吃的话味道非常苦，但如果煮熟了就不苦了。

2130
01:03:16.600 --> 01:03:20.260
They are poisonous either way, cooked or raw.
但无论生吃还是煮熟，它们都有毒。

2131
01:03:20.680 --> 01:03:22.540
Why would anyone cook them if they're poisonous?
既然有毒，为什么还会有人煮它们呢？

2132
01:03:22.900 --> 01:03:24.900
How do we even know what they taste like?
我们又是怎么知道它们是什么味道的？

2133
01:03:25.060 --> 01:03:26.040
I'll tell you.
我来告诉你。

2134
01:03:26.040 --> 01:03:35.220
Because a common poisoning technique would be to cook these mushrooms with non-poisonous mushrooms
因为一种常见的投毒手法就是把这些蘑菇和无毒的蘑菇一起煮，

2135
01:03:35.220 --> 01:03:37.160
and then feed them to your enemy.
然后喂给你的敌人吃。

2136
01:03:37.160 --> 01:03:42.000
And it's sort of like an undetectable way to poison someone to death.
这是一种让人难以察觉的毒杀手段。

2137
01:03:42.320 --> 01:03:43.820
So morbid.
太病态了。

2138
01:03:43.940 --> 01:03:45.580
So clearly this has been done.
所以显然有人这么干过。

2139
01:03:45.980 --> 01:03:46.220
Yeah.
是啊。

2140
01:03:46.620 --> 01:03:50.340
Did you see the movie Phantom Thread starring Daniel Day-Lewis?
你看过丹尼尔·戴-刘易斯主演的电影《魅影缝匠》吗？

2141
01:03:50.460 --> 01:03:52.340
Because this is a plot point in the movie.
因为这就是电影里的一个情节。

2142
01:03:52.680 --> 01:03:53.040
No.
没有。

2143
01:03:53.160 --> 01:03:56.780
And if you tell me to watch it, I'm going to watch the first 15 minutes of it.
而且如果你让我去看，我大概只会看前15分钟。

2144
01:03:56.960 --> 01:04:00.180
Well, you're going to miss the mushrooms because they happen later.
那你就会错过蘑菇的情节了，因为那是后面才发生的。

2145
01:04:00.720 --> 01:04:01.660
Let me tell you.
让我告诉你。

2146
01:04:01.880 --> 01:04:02.220
What?
什么？

2147
01:04:02.220 --> 01:04:04.540
Here's what happens to you if you eat these mushrooMs.
如果你吃了这些蘑菇，会发生什么。

2148
01:04:04.820 --> 01:04:04.960
Okay.
好吧。

2149
01:04:05.680 --> 01:04:06.320
Diarrhea.
腹泻。

2150
01:04:06.640 --> 01:04:07.020
Okay.
好吧。

2151
01:04:07.180 --> 01:04:07.740
Nausea.
恶心。

2152
01:04:08.380 --> 01:04:09.020
Vomiting.
呕吐。

2153
01:04:09.700 --> 01:04:10.340
Convulsions.
抽搐。

2154
01:04:11.020 --> 01:04:12.060
Impaired vision.
视力受损。

2155
01:04:12.720 --> 01:04:13.360
Paralysis.
瘫痪。

2156
01:04:13.720 --> 01:04:14.540
And collapse.
以及虚脱。

2157
01:04:14.940 --> 01:04:15.320
Jeez.
天哪。

2158
01:04:15.760 --> 01:04:19.860
It can take up to 5 to 10 hours before you get symptoMs.
症状可能需要5到10小时才会显现。

2159
01:04:20.300 --> 01:04:24.760
Now, most of the time, the symptoms will resolve themselves after a few days.
通常情况下，症状会在几天后自行消失。

2160
01:04:24.760 --> 01:04:26.300
But you get real sick.
但你会病得很重。

2161
01:04:26.480 --> 01:04:29.620
But they can cause death if you eat too many.
不过如果吃得太多，可能会导致死亡。

2162
01:04:29.960 --> 01:04:34.160
So guys, spoiler alert, Phantom Thread is an amazing movie.
伙计们，剧透预警，《魅影缝匠》是一部很棒的电影。

2163
01:04:34.380 --> 01:04:35.960
Everyone should watch it.
每个人都应该看看。

2164
01:04:36.120 --> 01:04:37.340
I'm not going to watch it.
我可不看。

2165
01:04:37.520 --> 01:04:41.100
As if anyone's ever going to take my movie recommendations again.
好像还会有人再听我的电影推荐似的。

2166
01:04:41.180 --> 01:04:44.120
I did watch this one all the way through twice.
这部电影我完整地看了两遍。

2167
01:04:44.260 --> 01:04:45.880
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

2168
01:04:46.460 --> 01:04:50.800
Stop listening here for 10 seconds if you don't want me to spoil the movie for you.
如果你不想被剧透，现在起跳过10秒。

2169
01:04:50.800 --> 01:04:55.380
So, but someone gets poisoned with mushrooMs.
总之，有人被蘑菇毒害了。

2170
01:04:55.840 --> 01:04:59.000
Do they have a little towel by their coffee pot?
他们的咖啡壶旁边有小毛巾吗？

2171
01:04:59.280 --> 01:05:06.520
No, but they have a wonderful English kitchen that looks like it's really fun to cook in.
没有，但他们有一个很棒的英式厨房，看起来在里面做饭一定很有趣。

2172
01:05:06.700 --> 01:05:09.080
So there is some great shots of a great kitchen.
所以里面有一些很棒的厨房镜头。

2173
01:05:09.320 --> 01:05:11.180
I'll be sure and check out the shots of the kitchen.
我一定会去看看那些厨房的镜头。

2174
01:05:11.680 --> 01:05:12.820
Oh, my God.
天哪。

2175
01:05:15.080 --> 01:05:16.000
Oh, dear.
天呐。

2176
01:05:16.000 --> 01:05:18.720
Let John Wick go, Angela.
放过疾速追杀吧，安吉拉。

2177
01:05:18.940 --> 01:05:19.720
Let it go.
算了吧。

2178
01:05:20.100 --> 01:05:23.660
Maybe once you get your Carvel cake, you'll forgive me.
也许等你吃到Carvel蛋糕，你就会原谅我了。

2179
01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:28.060
Once I join everyone who's ever celebrated their birthday at work or school.
等我加入那些在工作或学校过生日的人的行列之后吧。

2180
01:05:28.380 --> 01:05:32.180
Anyway, that is the download on the mushrooMs.
总之，这就是关于蘑菇的情况。

2181
01:05:32.580 --> 01:05:35.240
Well, you know the scene where Dwight tackles Michael to the ground?
你知道德怀特把迈克尔扑倒在地的那一幕吗？

2182
01:05:35.700 --> 01:05:35.900
Yeah.
知道。

2183
01:05:36.120 --> 01:05:38.900
There was much more of this in the deleted scenes.
删减片段里还有很多这样的内容。

2184
01:05:39.200 --> 01:05:42.080
There is a great talking head where Michael's like,
有一个很棒的访谈镜头，迈克尔说，

2185
01:05:42.080 --> 01:05:48.480
You know, when Dwight tackled me to the ground and was fishing the mushrooms out of my mouth with his finger.
你知道，当德怀特把我扑倒在地，用手指从我嘴里抠蘑菇的时候。

2186
01:05:48.760 --> 01:05:49.880
He like says it.
他就是这么说的。

2187
01:05:49.960 --> 01:05:51.800
He's like, when Dwight had his finger in my mouth.
他说，当德怀特的手指伸进我嘴里时。

2188
01:05:51.820 --> 01:05:59.080
He said, I laid back and I looked at the sky and the birds were chirping and there were clouds and it was so beautiful.
他说，我躺在那儿看着天空，鸟儿在鸣叫，云朵飘过，一切都那么美好。

2189
01:05:59.500 --> 01:06:02.700
And then I vomited because it was really gross.
然后我就吐了，因为那真的很恶心。

2190
01:06:03.040 --> 01:06:09.180
It's really funny that he had this sort of beautiful moment while Dwight was trying to fish the mushrooms out of his mouth.
他能在德怀特试图从他嘴里抠蘑菇的时候产生这种美好的瞬间，真是太搞笑了。

2191
01:06:09.180 --> 01:06:16.520
I have to ask, is that talking head, is he wearing his torn up clothes or is he wearing Dwight's sweatshirt?
我得问问，那个访谈镜头里，他穿的是那身破烂衣服，还是德怀特的运动衫？

2192
01:06:16.680 --> 01:06:24.540
No, it would have been like a wrap up talking head about his day and he was in his office with the Battlestar Galactica sweatshirt.
不，那应该是一个关于他这一天的总结访谈，他当时在办公室里，穿着那件《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》的运动衫。

2193
01:06:24.700 --> 01:06:28.600
Well, I love this idea that his clothes are tattered.
我喜欢他衣服破破烂烂的这个点子。

2194
01:06:28.780 --> 01:06:30.520
He's probably vomited on them.
他可能已经在衣服上吐过了。

2195
01:06:30.640 --> 01:06:35.140
And Dwight has to give him this rescue sweatshirt that was in his trunk.
然后德怀特不得不把后备箱里的那件备用运动衫给他穿。

2196
01:06:36.200 --> 01:06:45.820
Well, Jenna, I want you to know at 18 minutes, 31 seconds, when Dwight and Michael come back and they walk in the party and Michael immediately starts hitting those high notes,
珍娜，我想让你知道，在18分31秒，当德怀特和迈克尔回来走进派对，迈克尔立刻开始飙高音的时候，

2197
01:06:45.960 --> 01:06:46.080
right?
对吧？

2198
01:06:46.200 --> 01:06:47.300
He doesn't miss a beat.
他一点都没跑调。

2199
01:06:47.460 --> 01:06:56.240
The camera pans the conference room and Toby, Pam, Angela and Oscar are all standing together and they are smiling so big.
镜头扫过会议室，托比、帕姆、安吉拉和奥斯卡都站在一起，笑得特别开心。

2200
01:06:56.240 --> 01:07:02.140
And I thought, oh, my God, Toby and Angela are happy to see Michael and Oscar.
我当时想，天哪，托比和安吉拉见到迈克尔和奥斯卡居然这么高兴。

2201
01:07:02.720 --> 01:07:02.980
Yeah.
是啊。

2202
01:07:03.400 --> 01:07:09.960
Like, I expect Pam to smile at him, you know, but the fact that Toby and Angela were relieved to see Michael.
比如，我本以为帕姆会对他微笑，你知道的，但托比和安吉拉看到迈克尔回来时如释重负，这很有意思。

2203
01:07:10.180 --> 01:07:13.120
Well, they did not enjoy Jim being in charge.
嗯，他们确实不喜欢吉姆当负责人。

2204
01:07:13.480 --> 01:07:13.860
No.
没错。

2205
01:07:14.160 --> 01:07:16.940
We had a fan catch in this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，这一幕我们收到了粉丝提问。

2206
01:07:17.300 --> 01:07:17.460
Okay.
好的。

2207
01:07:17.460 --> 01:07:27.300
From Andrea T., who would like to know who made the peach cobbler for Creed because it's in a Pyrex dish.
来自安德烈·T，她想知道是谁给克里德做了桃子脆皮馅饼，因为那是装在派热克斯玻璃盘里的。

2208
01:07:27.440 --> 01:07:28.680
It's clearly homemade.
显然是自制的。

2209
01:07:28.980 --> 01:07:35.280
Did Angela go home and make this cobbler because she is so dedicated to throwing the perfect birthday party?
安吉拉是不是回家做了这个馅饼，因为她一心想举办一场完美的生日派对？

2210
01:07:35.460 --> 01:07:40.240
So, listen, I thought about this, too, and I think Angela did.
听着，我也想过这个问题，我觉得安吉拉确实做了。

2211
01:07:40.240 --> 01:07:48.980
I think when Creed said to Jim, tell Angela it's for Creed, she'll know what to do, Angela went home and made his favorite peach cobbler pie.
我想当克里德对吉姆说“告诉安吉拉这是给克里德的，她会知道该怎么做”时，安吉拉就回家做了他最爱的桃子脆皮馅饼。

2212
01:07:49.380 --> 01:07:50.320
I'm impressed.
我被惊艳到了。

2213
01:07:50.800 --> 01:07:51.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2214
01:07:51.440 --> 01:07:56.980
Well, at 18 minutes, 56 seconds, you guys, there is a great shot of the Fudgy the Whale cake.
伙计们，在18分56秒的时候，有一个“鲸鱼软糖”蛋糕的绝佳镜头。

2215
01:07:57.280 --> 01:07:58.560
Oh, so there you go.
哦，原来如此。

2216
01:07:58.640 --> 01:07:59.140
It was there.
它就在那儿。

2217
01:07:59.300 --> 01:08:00.000
Proof of Fudgy.
“鲸鱼软糖”的证据。

2218
01:08:00.200 --> 01:08:01.300
Proof of Fudgy.
“鲸鱼软糖”的证据。

2219
01:08:01.300 --> 01:08:11.840
And, Jenna, as we're wrapping up this scene, Jim and Michael have this fantastic moment where Jim is like, I tried to do all of their parties on one day.
珍娜，在这一幕快结束时，吉姆和迈克尔有一个很棒的瞬间，吉姆说他尝试把所有人的生日放在同一天过。

2220
01:08:11.980 --> 01:08:14.160
And Michael's like, oh, yeah, I did that.
然后迈克尔说，哦，是啊，我也干过那事。

2221
01:08:14.480 --> 01:08:15.500
Yeah, rookie mistake.
没错，新手常犯的错误。

2222
01:08:15.800 --> 01:08:16.880
You'll figure it out.
你会慢慢摸索出来的。

2223
01:08:17.240 --> 01:08:19.440
This scene is so beautiful.
这一幕太美好了。

2224
01:08:19.900 --> 01:08:26.840
It's this glimpse into Michael where he's kind of talking to a peer, right?
这让我们瞥见了迈克尔作为普通人的一面，他当时是在和同僚对话，对吧？

2225
01:08:26.840 --> 01:08:32.360
He's always manager-ing us or always wanting to be in that position of status to us.
他平时总是在管理我们，或者总是想在我们面前保持那种地位。

2226
01:08:32.440 --> 01:08:36.040
But here he is talking manager-on-manager to Jim.
但在这里，他是以经理对经理的身份在和吉姆交谈。

2227
01:08:36.480 --> 01:08:37.560
It's amazing.
太棒了。

2228
01:08:38.020 --> 01:08:39.020
It's so great.
真的太好了。

2229
01:08:39.120 --> 01:08:40.880
And it's such a human moment.
这是一个非常人性化的时刻。

2230
01:08:41.100 --> 01:08:43.140
You know, Jim's like, I'm not going to be here in 10 years.
你知道，吉姆说“我十年后不会待在这里了”。

2231
01:08:43.240 --> 01:08:44.660
And Michael's like, yeah, that's what I said.
迈克尔回答说“是啊，我当时也是这么说的”。

2232
01:08:44.840 --> 01:08:51.720
So as we close out this episode, Jenna, I thought we could hear just the final end of Jim and Michael's scene together.
那么在这一集结束之际，珍娜，我想我们可以听听吉姆和迈克尔最后那段对手戏的结尾。

2233
01:08:51.920 --> 01:08:52.900
Sam, can you play that?
萨姆，能放一下吗？

2234
01:08:54.920 --> 01:08:55.900
Sure glad you're back.
真高兴你回来了。

2235
01:08:56.740 --> 01:08:57.880
You are relieved.
你如释重负啊。

2236
01:08:58.420 --> 01:08:59.520
You have no idea.
你根本无法想象。

2237
01:09:01.000 --> 01:09:01.780
So what did I miss?
我错过了什么？

2238
01:09:02.660 --> 01:09:05.100
Well, I tried to put all the birthdays together at once.
嗯，我试着把所有人的生日放在一起过。

2239
01:09:05.280 --> 01:09:05.500
Oh.
哦。

2240
01:09:05.740 --> 01:09:07.020
So, terrible idea.
所以，真是个糟糕的主意。

2241
01:09:07.240 --> 01:09:07.940
Yeah, okay.
是啊，好吧。

2242
01:09:08.200 --> 01:09:08.840
I did that.
我干过那事。

2243
01:09:09.740 --> 01:09:10.600
Rookie mistake.
新手常犯的错误。

2244
01:09:11.020 --> 01:09:11.680
You did do it?
你真的干过？

2245
01:09:11.740 --> 01:09:12.120
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

2246
01:09:12.420 --> 01:09:12.640
Yeah.
是啊。

2247
01:09:13.740 --> 01:09:14.300
Let's wait.
等着瞧吧。

2248
01:09:14.860 --> 01:09:16.400
10 years, you'll figure it out.
十年后，你就会摸索出来的。

2249
01:09:17.240 --> 01:09:19.280
Well, I don't think I'll be here in 10 years.
嗯，我觉得我十年后不会待在这里了。

2250
01:09:21.160 --> 01:09:22.020
That's what I said.
我当时也是这么说的。

2251
01:09:27.400 --> 01:09:28.280
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

2252
01:09:32.240 --> 01:09:33.100
That's what who said?
那是谁说的？

2253
01:09:33.900 --> 01:09:34.540
I never know.
我从来都不知道。

2254
01:09:36.340 --> 01:09:37.280
Let's just say it.
我们就直说吧。

2255
01:09:38.580 --> 01:09:44.300
I say stuff like that, you know, to lighten the tension when things sort of get hard.
我会说那种话，你知道的，是为了在气氛有点紧张的时候缓和一下。

2256
01:09:44.520 --> 01:09:45.380
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

2257
01:09:46.780 --> 01:09:47.220
Hey.
嘿。

2258
01:09:47.220 --> 01:09:48.600
Nice.
不错。

2259
01:09:49.980 --> 01:09:51.180
Really good.
非常好。

2260
01:09:53.800 --> 01:09:56.600
Bravo, my young ward.
干得好，我的小徒弟。

2261
01:09:59.500 --> 01:10:00.620
I have a question.
我有个问题。

2262
01:10:01.060 --> 01:10:01.400
Yeah.
嗯。

2263
01:10:01.660 --> 01:10:04.760
Is Michael finally eating what was in the bag?
迈克尔终于在吃袋子里的东西了吗？

2264
01:10:06.240 --> 01:10:08.280
It sounds like he's eating nuts.
听起来他像是在吃坚果。

2265
01:10:08.920 --> 01:10:09.480
Yeah.
是啊。

2266
01:10:09.540 --> 01:10:13.820
I looked at it, and it's like, I can't tell what they are.
我看了看，就是，我看不出那是什么。

2267
01:10:14.020 --> 01:10:15.620
Little pretzel bites.
小块的椒盐卷饼。

2268
01:10:16.020 --> 01:10:17.460
You know what they look like?
你知道它们长什么样吗？

2269
01:10:17.460 --> 01:10:23.000
Like, if you get a Chex mix, there are these little stubby pretzel bite things.
就像如果你买了一包混合零食，里面会有那种短短的小块椒盐卷饼。

2270
01:10:23.300 --> 01:10:23.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

2271
01:10:24.040 --> 01:10:24.880
I don't know.
我不知道。

2272
01:10:25.020 --> 01:10:26.680
Or they look like slivered almonds.
或者它们看起来像杏仁片。

2273
01:10:27.060 --> 01:10:28.040
Or pecans.
或者是山核桃。

2274
01:10:28.040 --> 01:10:29.740
It's such a mystery.
真是个谜。

2275
01:10:30.220 --> 01:10:38.080
But as I watched that lovely scene that I absolutely love, I was wondering, what is he eating?
但当我看到那个我非常喜欢的可爱场景时，我在想，他到底在吃什么？

2276
01:10:39.820 --> 01:10:41.480
I'd forgotten about it.
我都快忘了这事了。

2277
01:10:41.900 --> 01:10:43.600
I'll have to go back and look.
我得回去看看。

2278
01:10:44.280 --> 01:10:44.520
Ah.
啊。

2279
01:10:44.960 --> 01:10:48.080
Well, you guys, that was Survivorman.
好了，伙计们，刚才那是《求生者》。

2280
01:10:48.320 --> 01:10:50.560
I don't think I'd make it out in the woods.
我觉得我没法在树林里生存下来。

2281
01:10:50.560 --> 01:10:52.820
I do think I'd make it at party planning.
但我确实觉得我能搞定派对策划。

2282
01:10:53.080 --> 01:10:55.240
I'd make sure everyone had their dang cake.
我会确保每个人都能吃到他们该死的蛋糕。

2283
01:10:56.240 --> 01:11:03.620
Next week, we have the deposition that has some of my favorite scenes of all time.
下周，我们将讨论那场证词陈述，里面有一些我个人最喜欢的场景。

2284
01:11:04.300 --> 01:11:04.840
Brilliant.
太棒了。

2285
01:11:05.380 --> 01:11:06.740
Thank you so much for listening.
非常感谢大家的收听。

2286
01:11:06.740 --> 01:11:09.420
Thank you for sending in your questions and your comments.
感谢大家发来的问题和评论。

2287
01:11:09.640 --> 01:11:10.380
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

2288
01:11:10.480 --> 01:11:11.540
We love you guys.
我们爱你们。

2289
01:11:12.140 --> 01:11:14.960
Everyone send Angela a cake on her birthday.
大家记得在安吉拉生日那天给她寄蛋糕。

2290
01:11:15.360 --> 01:11:16.720
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

2291
01:11:17.100 --> 01:11:18.360
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

2292
01:11:18.960 --> 01:11:19.360
All right.
好了。

2293
01:11:19.460 --> 01:11:19.960
Bye, guys.
再见，伙计们。

2294
01:11:20.220 --> 01:11:20.580
Bye.
再见。

2295
01:11:23.430 --> 01:11:26.010
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies' Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士》的“第二杯”。

